1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,519
In a 2024 test, an AI looked

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:04,980
at this clock and said: 9:30.

3
00:00:05,933 --> 00:00:06,813
It's quarter to six.

4
00:00:07,267 --> 00:00:09,286
Others said nine o'clock, or ten

5
00:00:09,287 --> 00:00:09,747
to five.

6
00:00:10,607 --> 00:00:13,126
Out of five AIs, only one

7
00:00:13,127 --> 00:00:13,927
got it right.

8
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:14,713
Why?

9
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:16,453
It swapped the hands.

10
00:00:17,093 --> 00:00:18,592
It read the long hand, on the

11
00:00:18,593 --> 00:00:20,852
nine, as the hour, and the short

12
00:00:20,853 --> 00:00:22,752
hand, near the six, as the

13
00:00:22,753 --> 00:00:22,993
minutes.

14
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:24,986
It's like someone describing a

15
00:00:24,987 --> 00:00:26,247
clock to you over the phone:

16
00:00:27,247 --> 00:00:28,966
"One hand near the nine, one

17
00:00:28,967 --> 00:00:30,887
near the six." Which is which?

18
00:00:31,607 --> 00:00:33,506
Guess wrong, and quarter to six

19
00:00:33,507 --> 00:00:34,527
becomes 9:30.

20
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,760
So when an AI sounds sure,

21
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:37,680
remember:
